{"task_id": "HumanEval/25", "solution": "from typing import List\ndef factorize(n: int) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"Return a list of prime factors for the given positive integer n.\n    Factors are in ascending order and listed by multiplicity.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 1:\n        return []\n\n    factors = []\n    temp_n = n\n\n    # Handle factor 2\n    while temp_n % 2 == 0:\n        factors.append(2)\n        temp_n //= 2\n\n    # Handle odd factors\n    d = 3\n    while d * d <= temp_n:\n        while temp_n % d == 0:\n            factors.append(d)\n            temp_n //= d\n        d += 2\n\n    # If temp_n is still greater than 1, it must be a prime factor itself\n    if temp_n > 1:\n        factors.append(temp_n)\n\n    return factors"}
