{"task_id": "HumanEval/40", "solution": "def triples_sum_to_zero(l: list):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if there are three distinct elements in the list that sum to zero.\n    Returns True if such a triplet exists, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(l)\n    if n < 3:\n        return False\n\n    nums = sorted(l) # Sort the list to efficiently find triplets using two pointers.\n\n    for i in range(n - 2):\n        if i > 0 and nums[i] == nums[i-1]: # Skip duplicates for the first element.\n            continue\n\n        left, right = i + 1, n - 1\n        while left < right:\n            current_sum = nums[i] + nums[left] + nums[right]\n\n            if current_sum == 0:\n                return True\n            elif current_sum < 0:\n                left += 1\n            else: # current_sum > 0\n                right -= 1\n    return False"}
