{"task_id": "HumanEval/82", "solution": "def prime_length(string):\n    \"\"\"Determines if the length of the given string is a prime number. Returns True if prime, False otherwise.\"\"\"\n    length = len(string)\n\n    if length < 2:\n        return False\n    i = 2\n    while i * i <= length:\n        if length % i == 0:\n            return False\n        i += 1\n    return True"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/83", "solution": "def starts_one_ends(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the count of n-digit positive integers that start or end with 1.\n    Assumes n is a positive integer (n >= 1).\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 1:\n        return 1\n    else:\n        # Applies the inclusion-exclusion principle formula for n > 1.\n        return (10 ** (n - 1)) + (8 * (10 ** (n - 2)))"}
