{"task_id": "HumanEval/93", "solution": "def encode(message):\n    \"\"\"\n    Encodes a message by swapping case and replacing vowels.\n    Vowels are replaced by letters two places ahead in the alphabet, preserving case.\n    \"\"\"\n    VOWELS_LOWER = {'a', 'e', 'i', 'o', 'u'}\n    VOWELS_UPPER = {'A', 'E', 'I', 'O', 'U'}\n    ALPHABET_LOWER = 'abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz'\n    ALPHABET_UPPER = 'ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ'\n\n    def _swap_case(char: str) -> str:\n        if char.islower():\n            return char.upper()\n        elif char.isupper():\n            return char.lower()\n        return char\n\n    def _replace_vowel(char: str) -> str:\n        # Assumes char is an alphabetic vowel (e.g., 'a', 'E') whose case should be preserved.\n        if char.islower():\n            alphabet = ALPHABET_LOWER\n        else:\n            alphabet = ALPHABET_UPPER\n        \n        index = alphabet.index(char)\n        new_index = (index + 2) % len(alphabet)\n        return alphabet[new_index]\n\n    encoded_chars = []\n    for char in message:\n        # First, apply case swapping to the character.\n        processed_char = _swap_case(char)\n\n        # Then, check if this *case-swapped* character is a vowel and replace it if so.\n        if processed_char in VOWELS_LOWER or processed_char in VOWELS_UPPER:\n            processed_char = _replace_vowel(processed_char)\n            \n        encoded_chars.append(processed_char)\n\n    return \"\".join(encoded_chars)"}
