{"task_id": "HumanEval/161", "solution": "def solve(s):\n    \"\"\"You are given a string s.\n    Processes the string based on letter presence and character case.\n    \"\"\"\n    \n    # FR2, Rule 3: Determine if the input string contains any letters.\n    # If no letters, reverse the entire string (FR3).\n    if not any(char.isalpha() for char in s):\n        return s[::-1]  # FR3, FR8: Reverse the string using slicing.\n    \n    # FR4: If 's' contains at least one letter, iterate through each character.\n    processed_chars = []\n    for char in s:\n        if char.isalpha():  # FR5: If it is a letter, reverse its case.\n            if char.islower():\n                processed_chars.append(char.upper())\n            else: # char.isupper()\n                processed_chars.append(char.lower())\n        else: # FR6: If not a letter, keep it unchanged.\n            processed_chars.append(char)\n            \n    # FR7, FR8: Concatenate the processed characters to form and return the result string.\n    return \"\".join(processed_chars)"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/160", "solution": "def do_algebra(operator: list[str], operand: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Constructs an algebraic expression from given operators and operands, then evaluates it.\n    Assumes valid inputs as per problem statement notes.\n    \"\"\"\n    expression_parts = []\n    # Interleave operands and operators to build the expression string.\n    for i in range(len(operand)):\n        expression_parts.append(str(operand[i]))\n        if i < len(operator):\n            expression_parts.append(operator[i])\n            \n    expression_string = \" \".join(expression_parts)\n    \n    # Evaluate the constructed expression string using Python's built-in eval().\n    result = eval(expression_string)\n    \n    return result"}
